# The only browser-visible setting. Every VITE_* value is public JavaScript, so the build
# rejects any other VITE_ variable (Vercel's automatic VITE_VERCEL_* metadata is allowed).
# Never put database URLs, encryption keys or SMTP settings here.
#
# Production uses /api/v1 on the same origin. An optional separate HTTPS API:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<backend-host>/api/v1     (https, ends in /api/v1, no trailing slash)
#
# Local development leaves it unset: requests go to /api/v1 and Vite proxies them to
# http://127.0.0.1:8000. For a local production-like build, copy this file to
# .env.production.local (ignored by Git) and set a loopback URL, for example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
